   206	def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
   207	    """
   208	    Stamp the source sprite onto every matching grey placeholder, erase the source, then let the stamped sprites settle downward under gravity.
   209	
   210	    Input structure:
   211	    - A black background contains one 4-connected multicolor source sprite and several 4-connected grey placeholder sprites.
   212	    - Every placeholder has the same normalized mask as the source sprite.
   213	    - Yellow obstacle components may appear near the bottom; they do not match or move.
   214	
   215	    Rule:
   216	    - Identify the unique multicolor source sprite and all grey placeholder components whose normalized masks match it.
   217	    - Copy the source sprite's per-cell colors onto each matching placeholder at the corresponding relative coordinates.
   218	    - Erase the original source sprite to black.
   219	    - Treat the newly colored placeholder copies as rigid sprites and apply simultaneous downward gravity until each is blocked by the bottom border, a settled sprite, or a yellow obstacle.
   220	
   221	    Key insight:
   222	    - The source sprite is both a color template and a temporary blocker: stamping happens before the source is erased, so understanding the erase-then-gravity order is necessary to reach the correct terminal layout.
   223	    """
